"""Nordstrom US category inventory, grouped by shopping department.

Source of truth: https://www.nordstrom.com/navigation-sitemap.xml (advertised
from the sitemap index at https://www.nordstrom.com/sitemap.xml and reachable
through the configured ScrapeOps residential proxy -- the storefront sits behind
PerimeterX and 403s on the plain/datacenter route). Refreshed 2026-10-14: 2,027
``/browse/<department>/...`` product-listing paths, of which the 1887 crawlable
shopping leaves below are kept across 30 departments.

Content, service, and policy sections that do not yield product listings are
excluded (``about``, ``customer-service``, ``services``, ``impact``, ``policy``,
``nordy-club``, ``content``, ``affiliate-program``, ``diversity-at-nordstrom``,
``support-black-owned-businesses``, and the ``load-test`` sentinel).

The Airflow DAG schedules one task per leaf and the GCS output path is the bare
leaf name, so leaf keys are the full ``<path>`` slug below ``/browse``
(``women-maternity-nursing-clothing``) -- globally unique for the many labels
that recur under several departments (``new``, ``shoes``, ``jewelry``, ...).
``-a category=<leaf>`` selects one listing; a department key such as ``women``
still resolves through the base class parent-selector support.
"""

